+The backend's existing device profiles can select the Q8 integer matrix route
+instead of the tile. Keys are `gguf_prefill_mxfp8/<format>/<N>x<K>/<epilogue>`;
+the four epilogues are `f32`, `bf16`, `bf16-add` and `bf16-silu`. Q8 overrides
+require whole 128-row tiles; unsupported formats, partial row tiles and other
+epilogues keep their existing route. A Q8 choice bypasses both FP8 kernels and
+the two-stage Lt path. T >= 1024 retains Lt irrespective of these profile keys.
+
+The first built-in set has 25 entries for the 36-SM RTX 5060 Ti, at exactly
+T=256. Two independent native calibrations measured 8 formats, 10 actual-model
+shapes and 4 epilogues; only Q8 winners confirmed in both runs were retained.
+Every run uses an 11-sample median, a 3% selection margin, interleaved confirmation
+and the existing 5% peak-output-difference rejection. The qualification test also
+uses an independent CPU/FP64 oracle. A win for one epilogue does not select the
+others. Other devices and unmeasured widths keep their previous choices; no
+5060 Ti SM-fill threshold is applied to them. User-calibrated profiles retain
+their normal per-key priority over built-ins.
+
+Adding this family does not discard previously calibrated non-FP8 routes. The
+loader recognizes only the verified additive catalog transition, excludes the
+new namespace from old provenance, and preserves unrelated old measurements
+when a partial FP8 calibration is stored. Missing provenance and other catalog
+mismatches retain their rejection behavior. Volta/Turing catalogs are unchanged.
+
+To measure this optional family on another supported device, set MXFP8=1 and run
+`ninfer-calibrate --only gguf_prefill_mxfp8/ --detail --repeat 11`.
+The normal profile schema, hardware/SM matching and route-catalog provenance
+apply. The family is skipped when MXFP8 is disabled or unsupported. Calibrate
+while the GPU is idle, then qualify full-model speed and quality before using
+the measured choices. Synthetic Op measurements alone do not prove a model win.
 
